---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import BackHome from '../../theme/BackHome.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Singing sand"
  description="A Chladni plate: drive a bolted square plate at a pitch, or sing to it, and watch sand gather on the lines that stay still."
>
  <BackHome />

  <div class="stage" data-plate>
    <div class="readout" aria-live="polite">
      <p class="hz" data-hz>&nbsp;</p>
      <p class="mode" data-mode>&nbsp;</p>
    </div>

    <div class="plate">
      <canvas class="wave" data-wave-layer hidden aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      <canvas class="sand" data-sand aria-label="A square plate covered in sand. Press to pour more."></canvas>
      <span class="bolt" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="controls">
      <div class="tuner">
        <button type="button" data-prev aria-label="Previous resonance">&lsaquo;</button>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="1000" step="1" aria-label="Pitch" data-freq />
        <button type="button" data-next aria-label="Next resonance">&rsaquo;</button>
      </div>
      <div class="toggles">
        <button type="button" data-sound aria-pressed="false">Sound off</button>
        <button type="button" data-sing aria-pressed="false">Sing to it</button>
        <button type="button" data-wave aria-pressed="false">Show the wave</button>
        <button type="button" data-scatter>Scatter</button>
      </div>
      <p class="status" data-status></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article>
    <h1>Singing sand</h1>
    <p>
      In 1787 Ernst Chladni sprinkled sand on a metal plate, clamped it at the centre, and drew a violin bow along its
      edge. The plate rang, and the sand ran off the parts that were shaking and piled up on the lines that weren't. Each
      note left a different figure.
    </p>
    <p>
      This plate is idealised. Each pattern is a pair of standing waves, <code>cos(nπx)·cos(mπy) ± cos(mπx)·cos(nπy)</code>,
      and its pitch grows with <code>n² + m²</code>, as a real square plate's does. Only the modes that are still at the
      centre are kept, since that's where the plate is bolted. Every mode answers the drive with a resonance peak, so
      between peaks the plate barely moves, and the sand stops where it is.
    </p>
    <p>
      The sand follows two rules. Each grain gets a random kick in proportion to how hard its spot is shaking, and it
      drifts a little downhill toward stiller plate. Nobody tells it where the lines are; it finds them.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Sing to it</strong> asks for your microphone. Your voice stays in the browser: the page finds its pitch by
      autocorrelation, matching the wave against itself to measure one period, and drives the plate at that frequency.
      The plate only moves while it hears a steady note. Use the arrows to jump straight to the next resonance, or press
      on the plate to pour more sand.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  import { startPlate } from './_app';

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-plate]');
  if (root) startPlate(root);
</script>

<style>
  .stage {
    --plate-size: min(88vw, calc(100dvh - 15rem), 42rem);
    --plate-edge: #3a4258;
    --plate-light: #262c40;
    --plate-dark: #10131f;

    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    align-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    min-height: 100dvh;
    padding: calc(var(--space-5) + var(--space-2)) var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 40%, var(--color-sky-bottom), var(--color-sky-top) 75%);
  }

  /* ---- readout -------------------------------------------------------------- */

  .readout {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .readout p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hz {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .mode {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    transition: color var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out);
  }

  [data-resonant] .mode {
    color: var(--color-relic);
  }

  /* ---- plate ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

  .plate {
    position: relative;
    width: var(--plate-size);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border: 1px solid var(--plate-edge);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background:
      linear-gradient(135deg, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.06), transparent 40%),
      radial-gradient(circle at 35% 30%, var(--plate-light), var(--plate-dark) 80%);
    box-shadow:
      0 24px 60px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.45),
      inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(255 255 255 / 0.04);
    transition: box-shadow var(--duration-slow) var(--ease-out);
  }

  [data-resonant] .plate {
    box-shadow:
      0 24px 60px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.45),
      0 0 40px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-relic) 25%, transparent),
      inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(255 255 255 / 0.04);
  }

  .plate canvas {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .sand {
    cursor: crosshair;
    touch-action: none;
  }

  .wave {
    image-rendering: auto;
  }

  .wave[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* The plate is bolted here, so every pattern is still at the centre. */
  .bolt {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: 3%;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border-radius: 50%;
    translate: -50% -50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 35% 35%, #8a93ab, #2a3044 70%);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* ---- controls --------------------------------------------------------------- */

  .controls {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    width: min(100%, 42rem);
  }

  .tuner {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .tuner input {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    accent-color: var(--color-relic);
  }

  .toggles {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  button {
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .tuner button {
    padding-inline: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  button:hover:not(:disabled) {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  button[aria-pressed='true'] {
    border-color: var(--color-relic);
    color: var(--color-relic);
  }

  button:disabled {
    opacity: 0.45;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .status {
    min-height: 1.4em;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ---- write-up --------------------------------------------------------------- */

  article {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-3);
  }

  article h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .mode,
    .plate {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
